  "body": "**CI repair. No research claim and no \u03ba change.** This is a two-line refresh of one stale source pin. It makes the `tests` group of *Verify research artifacts* pass again on main, and so on every open PR.\n\n## The failure (on unmodified main `0b1cccf8`)\n\n`make verify-tests` fails in `tests/test_single_intersection_spectrum_audit.py`, with 1 failure and 1 error:\n\n```\nspectrum_audit.AuditFailure: Changed pinned source: scripts/experiments/single_intersection.py\n```\n\n`verify.yml` runs this group on every push and pull request, so every PR based on current main shows `verify (3.11|3.13|3.14, tests)` as failing, whatever it changes. To reproduce on main:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B -m unittest tests.test_single_intersection_spectrum_audit\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `research/single-intersection-spectrum-audit` comes from #812 (ljste), integrated in `3b83e4f1`. It was built at base `66849e14`.\n- Its `SOURCE.json` pins `scripts/experiments/single_intersection.py` by whole-file SHA-256 at `08ddae46\u2026`, the pre-#778 version. `source_pins()` rejects any other digest.\n- #778 (merramil, \"2.09x faster exact single-intersection Gram replay\") then merged as `f015b04c` and rewrote that file. The new digest is `6874d41b\u2026`.\n- The audit's `SOURCE.json` already names #778 (head `f015b04c`) as an overlapping PR. Nobody refreshed the pin when it merged.\n\n## Why refreshing the pin is sound (the audit's evidence is unchanged)\n\n1. **#778 changed one function the audit never calls.** `git diff 66849e14 f015b04c -- scripts/experiments/single_intersection.py` is a single hunk in `minor_rows`. It packs the symmetric matrix into byte buffers instead of repeated big-int sums. The audit imports only `spectral_parity_bound` from this file, and that function is byte-identical.\n2. **`minor_rows` is behaviour-preserving anyway.** Old (`08ddae46`) and new (`6874d41b`) `minor_rows` return identical row lists for all 41 (h, k, j) cases of the audit's domain: 4 \u2264 h \u2264 10, 2 \u2264 k \u2264 min(4, \u230ah/2\u230b), 0 \u2264 j < k.\n3. **Every other output of the audit is unchanged.** With only the pin check bypassed, a fresh certificate equals the committed `RESULT.json` in every field. That covers 41 cases, 21 strict rank gaps, the characteristic polynomials, the controls and `implementation_sha256`. After the refresh, `spectrum_audit.py --write` changes exactly one line of `RESULT.json`: the same pin.\n\nThe diff is exactly two lines, replacing `08ddae46\u2026` with `6874d41b\u2026`:\n- `research/single-intersection-spectrum-audit/SOURCE.json`: `source_sha256[\"scripts/experiments/single_intersection.py\"]`;\n- `research/single-intersection-spectrum-audit/RESULT.json`: the same key, as regenerated by the audit's own `--write`.\n\n## Checks run\n\n- `python3 -B research/single-intersection-spectrum-audit/spectrum_audit.py` gives `PASS_LITERAL_BINARY_SPECTRAL_AUDIT`, with 41 cases.\n- `python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_single_intersection_spectrum_audit` gives 10 tests, OK.\n- `make verify-tests` (the full CI group) passes, and `git diff --exit-code` is then clean apart from the two intended lines.\n\nPoint 2 can be checked in a few seconds:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B - <<'EOF'\nimport subprocess, sys, types\nfrom itertools import combinations\nsys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nimport experiments.single_intersection as new\nold = types.ModuleType('old')\nexec(subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', '66849e14:scripts/experiments/single_intersection.py']).decode(), old.__dict__)\ncases = [(h, k, j) for h in range(4, 11) for k in range(2, min(4, h // 2) + 1) for j in range(k)]\nfor h, k, j in cases:\n    L = [sum(1 << i for i in c) for c in combinations(range(h), k)]\n    assert old.minor_rows(L, j) == new.minor_rows(L, j)\nprint('identical on', len(cases), 'cases')\nEOF\n```\n\n## What this PR deliberately does not touch (maintainer-signed evidence)\n\n- **frontier890 coverage.** `research/community-frontier890-audit/CONTENT-COVERAGE.json` records `integrated_sha256` for these two files: `RESULT.json` `9cb2210e\u2026` and `SOURCE.json` `610fb988\u2026`. `scripts/verify_pr_reconciliation.py` re-checks those digests against the live files. So after this PR, the frontier890 row for #812 needs re-signing. That record is in turn bound by `docs/research/community-frontier890-integration.json` and several efficient300/500 check receipts. I did not rewrite maintainer-signed records.\n\n  The check is masked on main today: `verify_pr_reconciliation.py` already stops earlier, at the stale `Makefile` pin below.\n- **Two other stale pins on main.** Both are path-filtered workflows, so they don't run on ordinary PRs. They are listed only for completeness and are not changed here:\n  - `research/community-reconciliation92-audit/MANIFEST.json` pins `Makefile` at `ea8830dd\u2026`. It has drifted since the 2026-10-14 integration commits (`14c101c9` onward), and `community-reconciliation92-audit/verify.py` fails with \"Changed integrated source: Makefile\".\n  - `research/r420-two-sided-basis/SOURCES.json` pins `certificates/selected-result.json`. It has drifted since `0a31ad88` (batch1099 checkpoint 1), and its verifier rejects with \"source pin: certificates/selected-result.json\".\n- **The preserved-research manifest.** `docs/research/preserved-research-manifest.json` keeps `original_sha256 = 08ddae46\u2026`. That is a historical \"original\" record, so it is correct as is.\n\nCredit: the audit is ljste's (#812) and the speed-up is merramil's (#778). This PR only re-pins.\n\n## Disclosure\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar (thakrarsagar) with substantial AI assistance from Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code. Apache-2.0.\n",
